        "id": 1000007
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-07-26T20:56:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "These fields where not present in the specs that came out of the design meeting. I agree we\u0027ll need to somehow connect a ServiceInstance to a Network, but what\u0027s the reason for connecting it to a Service (this is a confusing point for anyone using CORD, so we should do our best to address it)",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 484,
        "startChar": 5,
        "endLine": 485,
        "endChar": 72
      },
      "revId": "9141248ca0acbd3dabc1d1920e4ddc5f51b8bf40",
      "serverId": "2a2bfe1b-c5c2-48ed-9ac8-16438ab24388",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1a1a2d67_673c7a94",
        "filename": "xos/core/models/core.xproto",
        "patchSetId": 27
      },
      "lineNbr": 485,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000016
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-07-26T21:06:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This was discussed between Jono and myself during the OpenCloud meeting today, using the ONOS service as an example. The unit of tenancy (aka \"ServiceInstance\") of the ONOS service is the App. The VTN Service uses the ONOS App. This requires a link from Service to ServiceInstance. \n\nThe link from Network to ServiceInstance is something I hope we can eliminate, possibly during further refactoring of the vrouter service.",
      "parentUuid": "1a1a2d67_27cfa2b2",
